# Add any directories, files, or patterns you don't want to be tracked by version control
bin
obj
# Test run output: TRX result files and blame's sequence/dump files. Every suite writes one now, locally and
# in CI, so a failure always leaves an artifact behind instead of having to be reproduced first.
TestResults
# Code coverage: the per-suite raw slices and the merged report. Regenerated by any `dotnet test` run,
# and the raw slices are large binary blobs.
artifacts
.ionide
*.log
*.bak
node_modules

.claude\.settings.local.json
.fake
tmp

.vscode
.aiworkdata

# Exclude IHC project files.
.\*.vis

# Important to exclude - user config file - contains secrets. The glob also covers the
# ihcsettings.json.tmp that ihc_settings_encrypt swaps through and that a kill can strand, which
# holds the same password. The tracked ihcsettings_example/_template files are named with an
# underscore and are deliberately outside it.
ihcsettings.json*
.mcp.json

# Pinned Opengrep ruleset, cloned by scripts/opengrep-scan.sh.
.opengrep-rules
